`DisallowExternalBeatmapRulesetChanges` was *designed* for exactly this purpose. See this existing code:

https://github.com/ppy/osu/blob/77b4bd97f8a73f0c404a56ff408250af3cd671b0/osu.Game/Screens/Edit/EditorLoader.cs#L65-L66

The reason it's not working is an added complication from `SongSelect`, which is caching its own decoupled ruleset bindable over the game global one:

https://github.com/ppy/osu/blob/77b4bd97f8a73f0c404a56ff408250af3cd671b0/osu.Game/Screens/Select/SongSelect.cs#L353-L354

and then attempts to sync it with the global one, which is the root failure here:

https://github.com/ppy/osu/blob/77b4bd97f8a73f0c404a56ff408250af3cd671b0/osu.Game/Screens/Select/SongSelect.cs#L809-L810

This is a bit awkward, but can be bypassed by doing something like this:

```diff
diff --git a/osu.Game/Screens/Edit/EditorLoader.cs b/osu.Game/Screens/Edit/EditorLoader.cs
index 0a2b8437fa..64a77c39f4 100644
--- a/osu.Game/Screens/Edit/EditorLoader.cs
+++ b/osu.Game/Screens/Edit/EditorLoader.cs
@@ -64,6 +64,7 @@ protected override void LoadComplete()
 
             // will be restored via lease, see `DisallowExternalBeatmapRulesetChanges`.
             Mods.Value = Array.Empty<Mod>();
+            Ruleset.Value = Beatmap.Value.BeatmapInfo.Ruleset;
         }
 
         protected virtual Editor CreateEditor() => new Editor(this);
diff --git a/osu.Game/Screens/Select/SongSelect.cs b/osu.Game/Screens/Select/SongSelect.cs
index 8870239485..1755fcc2a8 100644
--- a/osu.Game/Screens/Select/SongSelect.cs
+++ b/osu.Game/Screens/Select/SongSelect.cs
@@ -806,7 +806,17 @@ private void bindBindables()
 
             Ruleset.ValueChanged += r => updateSelectedRuleset(r.NewValue);
 
-            decoupledRuleset.ValueChanged += r => Ruleset.Value = r.NewValue;
+            decoupledRuleset.ValueChanged += r =>
+            {
+                bool wasDisabled = Ruleset.Disabled;
+
+                // a sub-screen may have taken a lease on the decoupled ruleset bindable,
+                // which will disable both the decoupled bindable and the game-global bindable (via the `DisabledChanged` callback below).
+                // to make sure changes sync without crashes, lift the disable for a second to sync, and then restore the old value.
+                Ruleset.Disabled = false;
+                Ruleset.Value = r.NewValue;
+                Ruleset.Disabled = wasDisabled;
+            };
             decoupledRuleset.DisabledChanged += r => Ruleset.Disabled = r;
 
             Beatmap.BindValueChanged(workingBeatmapChanged);
```

which I think is still better than what you have here, but I'm going to wait for further opinions to make sure there's agreement on that.
